    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T11:44:28Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the report and the screenshots, @vilts.\n\n**Triage (maintainer side):**\n- **Labels:** `bug`, `P1` (wrong behaviour a user hits) and `area:ui`. Claim recorded for @mkinney - label and assignee set (only collaborators can set labels; your comment is the claim).\n- **Version:** the orthographic view first shipped in 0.16.0 (PR #455), so it isn't in 0.10.0. Could you check the version in the top-right corner of the toolbar (or Help > About) and confirm which build you saw this in?\n- **Likely already fixed on main:** PR #604 (`5acd75c`, merged 2026-11-10) maps the orthographic depth into WebGPU's clip range instead of OpenGL's. With the old mapping, half the depth range was clipped, so a part could vanish when switching to Ortho - what your screenshots show. PR #613 (also merged 2026-11-10) fixes the ortho rays for the traced stock and picking. Neither is in a release yet; both ship in the next minor (0.17.0).\n- **For @mkinney's fix:** reproduce on current main first. If #604 already fixes it, close this as done in `5acd75c` with a camera test that pins it (part stays in view after the switch, perspective and ortho, for a framed STEP model). If it still vanishes, the remaining suspect is the ortho extent or near/far planes when framing.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
